      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Place the bulgur wheat in a large heatproof bowl. Pour over 350ml of just-boiled water, stir briefly, then cover tightly with a plate or cling film. Leave for 15 minutes until the water is fully absorbed."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "In a small bowl, mix together the tomato puree, olive oil, pomegranate molasses, lemon juice and sumac to make the dressing."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Fluff the soaked bulgur with a fork. While it is still warm, pour over the dressing and mix thoroughly so every grain is coated."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the tomato, red pepper, spring onion, parsley, mint and black pepper. Toss everything together. Taste and adjust salt, lemon and pomegranate molasses."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Leave to rest for at least 10 minutes before serving to allow the flavours to come together. Serve at room temperature."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Bulgur is stodgy and clumping"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the dressing while the bulgur is still warm. Warm grains separate much more easily and absorb the dressing evenly. Fluff with a fork before dressing rather than stirring with a spoon."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Kisir tastes too sweet"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pomegranate molasses varies in sweetness between brands. Add half first, taste, then adjust. Extra lemon juice or sumac will bring the sourness back into balance."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Salad looks dry after resting"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The bulgur continues absorbing liquid as it sits. Add a drizzle more olive oil and a squeeze of lemon just before serving to freshen it up."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Kisir is the Turkish equivalent of tabbouleh, but built around a richer, more intensely flavoured dressing. The use of "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "sumac-term"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "sumac"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and pomegranate molasses alongside the lemon gives it a layered sourness that straight lemon juice alone cannot achieve. It is eaten across southeastern Turkey in particular, and is one of the first salads to appear at meze tables. It keeps well in the fridge and is better the next day once the bulgur has fully absorbed all the dressing."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
